<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fortezza da Basso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1534">1534</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fortezza da Basso is a fortress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> built from 1534 for Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-de-medici">Alessandro de' Medici</a> to designs by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-da-sangallo-the-younger">Antonio da Sangallo the Younger</a>. Placed to overawe the citizens rather than to defend against outside enemies, it symbolised the end of republican Florence. It is now used as an exhibition centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fortezza-da-basso.jpg" alt="Fortezza da Basso" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fortezza_da_basso,_ingresso_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
